            <description><![CDATA[<h2>Jarvis is the Focus screen now</h2>

<p>This update removes everything that was not the day in front of you. The app
is <strong>39 MB instead of 619 MB</strong>, and the first launch shrinks your
message database by dropping the search index it no longer needs — on the
machine this was built against, 49 MB became 3.4 MB. Nothing you have is
deleted: every message, task and note stays exactly where it was.</p>

<h3>What is gone</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>The Context Hub screen.</strong> Sources are connected and repaired
      in Settings (⌘,), where they have lived for a while. Meetings moved to the
      capsule in Focus's title bar, and to a Meetings row in the menu-bar menu.</li>
  <li><strong>The on-device search index and its 559 MB model.</strong> That is
      the whole size difference. Finding your tasks never used it — the finder
      reads Slack and Teams live, and Gmail and meetings through your own
      history.</li>
  <li><strong>The coding-agent surface:</strong> the local MCP server on port
      8765, the <code>jarvis</code> command line tool, and the Claude Code
      plugin. <em>If you pointed Claude Code or another agent at Jarvis, that
      connection stops working in this version.</em></li>
</ul>

<h3>What is unchanged</h3>
<p>Focus and your day, the task finder, priorities and house rules, Tell Jarvis,
Slack and Microsoft Teams as live sources, Gmail, Google Calendar, meeting
capture with transcription and speaker names, and the morning greeting.</p>
]]></description>
